---
title: "07a  From obligation to payment: who certifies what (goods, services and works of a national agency)"
---
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  %% QUESTION THIS DIAGRAM ANSWERS: for one payment to a supplier, which officer certifies which fact, in which document, and which checks are made by someone outside the agency before the money leaves?
  %% WHAT THE DIAGRAM SHOWS: every certification before step 15 is made by an officer of the agency itself. The first outside check is by the servicing bank (step 15). The bank checks signatures, account details and the cash limit. It does not check the delivery. COA examines after payment.
  %% SOURCES: obligation request (ORS) boxes and fields [ORS-FORM]. Obligations are entered in registries, not in the journal [GAM-GUIDE][JC2019-1]. Voucher boxes A to D [DV-BOXES]. Due and demandable = delivered and accepted [JC2019-1]. LDDAP-ADA fields [LDDAP-FORM]. LDDAP-ADA and its summary list (SLIIE), four copies, copy to BTr the same day [CL2013-16A]. Credit to payee in 24 to 48 hours through eMDS [eMDS]. Journal entries for payment and tax withheld [GAM-GUIDE]. Tax Remittance Advice listed as a disbursement authority [NBC599]. Audit after payment [COA2011-002]. System controls of BTMS in the last note [BTMS-SITE][CL2025-8].
  %% GENERAL KNOWLEDGE, NOT OPENED IN A SOURCE HERE: the exact wording of Box A and Box B of the ORS, the names of the inspection documents in steps 4 to 6, step 19 (bank report of items paid and not paid), step 22 (update of the registry), the sending of paid vouchers to the auditor in step 23.
  participant EU as Requesting<br/>(end-user) unit
  participant BUD as Budget<br/>unit
  participant SUP as Supplier or<br/>contractor
  participant INS as Inspection committee<br/>and property unit
  participant ACC as Accounting<br/>unit
  participant HEAD as Head of agency or<br/>authorized official
  participant CASH as Cash<br/>unit
  participant GSB as Servicing bank<br/>(MDS)
  participant BTR as BTr<br/>and BSP
  participant BIR as BIR
  participant COA as COA<br/>auditor

  Note over EU,SUP: COMMIT. The contract is signed (chapter 06). The agency records the obligation.
  EU->>BUD: Obligation Request and Status (ORS) with the contract.<br/>Box A: the requesting head certifies that the charge<br/>is necessary and lawful and the documents are valid
  BUD->>BUD: Box B: allotment is available and obligated for this purpose.<br/>ORS number assigned. Entry in the registry of<br/>allotments, obligations and disbursements. No journal entry<br/>#nbsp;

  Note over EU,INS: VERIFY. The claim becomes due and demandable only after delivery and acceptance.
  SUP->>EU: Delivery or work accomplished, with invoice or billing
  EU->>INS: Request for inspection
  INS-->>EU: Inspection and acceptance report,<br/>or certified statement of work accomplished
  INS->>INS: Property unit receives goods and updates property records<br/>#nbsp;

  Note over EU,HEAD: APPROVE THE CLAIM. One disbursement voucher (DV), four signatures.
  EU->>ACC: DV with supporting documents. Box A: the officer with direct<br/>supervision and knowledge of the facts certifies the claim
  ACC->>ACC: Examine documents. Compute tax to withhold, retention, damages.<br/>Box B: accounting entry. Box C: cash available,<br/>documents complete, amount proper<br/>#nbsp;
  ACC->>ACC: Journal entry voucher (JEV): debit expense or asset,<br/>credit accounts payable<br/>#nbsp;
  ACC->>HEAD: DV for approval
  HEAD-->>ACC: Box D: approved for payment

  Note over ACC,BIR: PAY. The payment order is the LDDAP-ADA: a list of payees, bank accounts, ORS numbers and net amounts.
  ACC->>HEAD: LDDAP-ADA and its summary list (SLIIE),<br/>certified by the head of accounting
  HEAD-->>CASH: Approved LDDAP-ADA and SLIIE
  CASH->>GSB: LDDAP-ADA and SLIIE (paper, or through eMDS)
  GSB->>GSB: Check signatures, account details and the NCA balance.<br/>Debit the MDS sub-account of the agency<br/>#nbsp;
  GSB->>SUP: Credit the payee account with the net amount
  GSB->>BTR: Copy of the SLIIE on the same day
  BTR-->>GSB: Replenishment from the Treasury Single Account
  GSB-->>CASH: Items paid, and items not paid (to be invalidated)
  ACC->>BIR: Tax withheld, by Tax Remittance Advice (no cash moves)
  ACC->>ACC: JEV for the payment: debit accounts payable,<br/>credit Cash-MDS and Due to BIR<br/>#nbsp;
  BUD->>BUD: Registry updated: disbursement, and unpaid balance of the obligation<br/>#nbsp;

  Note over ACC,COA: AFTER PAYMENT
  ACC->>COA: Paid vouchers with supporting documents, and the copy of the SLIIE
  COA-->>HEAD: Audit observations, or notices of suspension or disallowance (chapter 09)

  Note over EU,COA: IN AGENCIES THAT USE BTMS: obligation request, purchase order, goods received note, voucher and journal entry are records in one system.<br/>The system refuses an obligation above the allotment and a payment above the cash allocation, and it creates the journal entry from the voucher.
